---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import MobileMenu from '../components/layout/MobileMenu.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import Divider from '../components/ui/Divider.astro';
import Contact from '../components/sections/Contact.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const breadcrumbLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Pricing', path: '/pricing' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pricing · Winters Code"
  description="One price, everything in. Local business sites start at $1,750 with photos, copy, branding, top Google scores, and security all included. Care plans optional from $75/mo. No tiers, no surprise add-ons."
  canonicalPath="/pricing"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <Header />
  <MobileMenu />

  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Pricing"
    h1="One price. Everything in."
    sub="Local business sites start at $1,750, with everything below included. Bigger jobs cost more and I tell you up front. Care plans optional, from $75 a month."
    bgImage="/photo/local/scenes/seastacks-gorse"
    showcase
    bgPosition="center 50%"
  />

  <Divider label="01" />

  <section class="pr-intro" aria-label="How pricing works">
    <p class="pr-lead">
      The low-priced sites you see advertised, the few-hundred-dollar ones, are
      real. But that is the starting point, not the finish line. The pages, the
      photos, the contact form, the words, those come as add-ons, and the real
      total shows up one line at a time. I price it the other way: one number,
      all-in, nothing buried.
    </p>
    <p class="pr-lead">
      Here is the honest range. National agencies typically start around
      <strong>$5,000</strong> and run six weeks or more. Hourly freelancers often
      run <strong>$2,500</strong> and up over a month. A Winters Code site starts at
      <strong>$1,750</strong>. The same modern stack and quality bar, for less than a
      freelancer, and live in days, not months.
    </p>
    <p class="pr-lead">
      Everything below is included. No per-page fees, no surprise
      add-ons, no monthly anything you didn't ask for. The price I quote is the
      price you pay. Every project starts with a free consult and a written quote
      that holds for 14 days. A 50 percent deposit locks scope and schedule, and
      the rest is due at launch.
    </p>
    <p class="pr-lead">
      One thing worth doing before you hire anyone, including me. Ask them to
      show you the Google score on their own website. It is free, it takes about
      thirty seconds, and it is the same test I ran on 219 businesses in this
      county. Mine are on <a href="/wall">the wall</a>, live, updated on their
      own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Divider label="02" />

  <section class="pr-block" aria-labelledby="pr-incl-h">
    <h2 class="pr-h" id="pr-incl-h">Every site, $1,750</h2>
    <p class="pr-sub">A real, finished website, not a demo you keep buying pieces of.</p>
    <article class="pr-card pr-incl">
      <ul class="pr-feat pr-feat--2">
        <li>A custom site made for your business, not a template with your name dropped in</li>
        <li>The core pages you need, with all the words written for you</li>
        <li>Real photos. Bill Bailey or I come shoot your business, no stock</li>
        <li>A logo and brand if you don't have one, with real vector files for signs, shirts, and print</li>
        <li>Top Google scores for speed and search, proven on Google's own test. Most cheap sites sit near 60 on a phone</li>
        <li>Found by Google and the new AI assistants. Scrapers and junk bots shut out</li>
        <li>Your website, Google listing, and socials all lined up and pointing the same way</li>
        <li>Real security baked in: HTTPS, a hardened setup, and spam-protected forms</li>
        <li>Email on your own domain, a contact form that reaches you, and privacy and terms pages</li>
        <li>No lock-in, no contract, no required monthly fee. When it's done, it's yours to keep</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="pr-incl-foot">Want it line by line? See the full breakdown on <a href="/services">services</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <Divider label="03" />

  <section class="pr-block" aria-labelledby="pr-own-h">
    <h2 class="pr-h" id="pr-own-h">What "yours to keep" actually means</h2>
    <p class="pr-sub">Most website deals never say this part out loud. Here it is plainly.</p>
    <article class="pr-card pr-incl">
      <ul class="pr-feat">
        <li>The domain is registered in your name. I never hold it. If you and I never speak again, you still own the address</li>
        <li>The site runs on your own Cloudflare account. At this size that tier costs nothing</li>
        <li>I hold an access token you can revoke in two clicks, any day, without asking me</li>
        <li>The code is yours, and it moves to your own GitHub whenever you want it</li>
        <li>Skip the care plan and nothing turns off. The site keeps running exactly as it is</li>
        <li>The care plan buys changes, monitoring, and somebody local to call. It does not buy access to your own website. You already have that</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <p class="pr-foot">
      If you pay monthly or yearly for a managed website, multiply it by five
      before you compare it to anything else. That is what the next five years
      costs you. At the end of it, ask what you own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Divider label="04" />

  <section class="pr-block" aria-labelledby="pr-more-h">
    <h2 class="pr-h" id="pr-more-h">When it costs more</h2>
    <p class="pr-lead">
      The floor covers a complete core site. These add to it, and I quote them
      clearly: bigger sites with a lot more pages, SEO expansion for more reach
      and local search, online booking, payments, or a store, and listing feeds
      like MLS or RMLS for real estate. Cross-platform apps and custom systems
      are quoted per project too. Tell me what you need and I'll price it
      straight.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Divider label="05" />

  <section class="pr-block" aria-labelledby="pr-care-h">
    <h2 class="pr-h" id="pr-care-h">Care plans</h2>
    <p class="pr-sub">Optional. Fixed monthly pricing, public. Cancel anytime.</p>
    <div class="pr-grid pr-grid-2">
      <article class="pr-card pr-care">
        <h3 class="pr-card-h">Basic</h3>
        <p class="pr-price">starting at <strong>$75</strong><span>/mo</span></p>
        <ul class="pr-feat"><li>Hosting and SSL, managed on your account</li><li>Daily backups</li><li>Security patches</li><li>10 content edits / month</li><li>Uptime monitoring</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article class="pr-card pr-care">
        <h3 class="pr-card-h">Pro</h3>
        <p class="pr-price">starting at <strong>$250</strong><span>/mo</span></p>
        <ul class="pr-feat"><li>Everything in Basic</li><li>Unlimited reasonable edits</li><li>Priority same-day turnaround</li><li>Quarterly performance + SEO pass, fixes made</li><li>Improvements rolled in as you grow</li></ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="pr-foot">
      Not required, ever. The site is yours either way. See <a href="/website-maintenance">care plan details</a> or <a href="/services">all services</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Divider label="06" />

  <Contact sectionNumber="06" centered suppressHeader />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pr-intro { padding: 24px 4px 8px; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-intro { padding: 36px 4px 12px; } }
  .pr-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-lead { font-size: 17px; } }
  .pr-lead strong { color: var(--color-ash-100); font-weight: 600; }

  .pr-block { padding: 28px 4px 20px; max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-block { padding: 40px 4px 28px; } }
  .pr-h {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-h { font-size: 36px; } }
  .pr-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .pr-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; margin: 18px 0 0; }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; } .pr-grid-2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  .pr-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--copper-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card, 10px);
    padding: 18px 16px 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .pr-card-h {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ash-100);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .pr-time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-copper);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .pr-feat {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--color-ash-300);
    line-height: 1.6;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }
  .pr-feat li { padding: 3px 0 3px 14px; position: relative; }
  .pr-feat li::before { content: "·"; position: absolute; left: 2px; top: 1px; color: var(--color-copper); font-weight: 700; }
  .pr-feat--2 li { break-inside: avoid; }
  @media (min-width: 740px) { .pr-feat--2 { columns: 2; column-gap: 30px; } }
  .pr-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pr-incl-foot {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
    margin: 14px 0 0;
  }
  .pr-incl-foot a {
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.4);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .pr-care .pr-price {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .pr-care .pr-price strong {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 34px;
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 2px;
  }
  .pr-care .pr-price span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
  }
  .pr-foot {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-ash-400);
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .pr-foot a {
    color: var(--color-wc-green);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(77, 216, 168, 0.4);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
